From 592480825fdbb9557cfa0be2ff5fba743ba86eee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: broody <broody@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:40:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Bounded mode: streamed commitments (16 columns at a
 time), switchable

A column-provider leaf builder (MerkleOpsLifted::build_leaves_with_column_provider:
a materializing default, and a streamed SIMD Blake2s override that holds one packed
state per 16 rows and one 16-column block at a time), MerkleProverLifted::
commit_with_column_provider and decommit_with_queried_values. In bounded mode the PCS
builds trees with CommitmentTreeProver::new_streamed and rebuilds them for openings the
same way, capturing queried values per block; the Cairo and circuit preprocessed trees
too. CommitmentSchemeProver::set_streamed_commitments(false) keeps whole-tree builds.

Streamed leaves, layers, roots and openings equal the ordinary ones (CPU and SIMD)
across sizes, lifts and block/lane boundaries; bounded circuit proofs equal unbounded
ones in both settings. On the policy-note PIE: 51.7 GiB default, 27.8 GiB bounded
(whole trees), 22.0 GiB streamed; every proof byte-identical and verified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
